00:02:19,626 --> 00:02:21,431
What is it, really?

30
00:02:21,967 --> 00:02:28,689
A label is a key-value pair of metadata attached to an image, a container, a network or a volume.

31
00:02:28,689 --> 00:02:34,371
Docker itself ignores labels; people and tools use them to answer "what is this?":

32
00:02:34,371 --> 00:02:38,113
which source code and version an image was built from,

33
00:02:38,113 --> 00:02:42,340
which team owns a container, which environment it belongs to.

34
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:48,646
Filters (--filter label=…) then select objects by label for listing, monitoring or cleanup.

