113
00:09:03,133 --> 00:09:06,678
What should I know about multi-architecture images?

114
00:09:07,233 --> 00:09:12,713
A container image contains machine code for one CPU architecture:

115
00:09:12,713 --> 00:09:19,036
an amd64 (x86-64) binary does not run on an arm64 processor (Apple silicon,

116
00:09:19,036 --> 00:09:22,914
AWS Graviton, Raspberry Pi) without emulation.

117
00:09:22,914 --> 00:09:26,961
A multi-architecture image is one name, one tag,

118
00:09:26,961 --> 00:09:34,043
with a variant per platform behind it (an image index, also called a manifest list).

119
00:09:34,043 --> 00:09:41,040
docker pull and docker run pick the variant that matches the machine automatically.

120
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:46,773
docker buildx build --platform … builds all variants in one command.

121
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:52,493
First, a fresh practice folder for this lesson.

