147
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:57,825
Can you show me build cache optimization?

148
00:11:58,367 --> 00:12:01,191
Lesson 039 explained the build cache:

149
00:12:01,191 --> 00:12:06,077
a step is reused when it and everything before it are unchanged.

150
00:12:06,077 --> 00:12:09,741
This lesson applies it to make real builds fast:

151
00:12:09,741 --> 00:12:09,893
1.

152
00:12:09,893 --> 00:12:13,710
Order steps from least to most frequently changed:

153
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:15,618
dependencies before code.

154
00:12:15,618 --> 00:12:15,771
2.

155
00:12:17,533 --> 00:12:21,493
First, a fresh practice folder for this lesson.

156
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:24,423
Build the before version twice.

157
00:12:24,423 --> 00:12:28,894
The second time, nothing changed, so everything is cached:

158
00:12:28,894 --> 00:12:35,293
Now change one line of the application code, as every commit does, and build again:

159
00:12:35,833 --> 00:12:41,795
Now change one line of the application code, as every commit does, and build again:

160
00:12:41,795 --> 00:12:42,226
COPY .

161
00:12:42,226 --> 00:12:42,298
.

162
00:12:42,298 --> 00:12:45,890
changed, so the dependency installation ran again:

163
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:52,499
every package was downloaded and installed for a change that did not touch the dependencies.

164
00:12:52,499 --> 00:12:55,013
Do the same with the after version:

165
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:56,010
COPY .

166
00:12:56,010 --> 00:12:56,083
.

167
00:12:56,083 --> 00:12:59,774
changed, so the dependency installation ran again:

168
00:12:59,774 --> 00:13:06,565
every package was downloaded and installed for a change that did not touch the dependencies.

169
00:13:06,565 --> 00:13:09,148
Do the same with the after version:

170
00:13:09,148 --> 00:13:10,846
Only the last step ran.

171
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,067
Let me try something.

172
00:13:14,067 --> 00:13:20,984
A teammate adds the build time to the image, at the top of the Dockerfile where it is easy to find.

173
00:13:21,533 --> 00:13:26,320
Find the first step that ran; everything after it runs because of it.

174
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,569
Here it is step 2:

175
00:13:27,569 --> 00:13:29,928
RUN echo "built at ${BUILD_TIME}".

176
00:13:29,928 --> 00:13:35,340
An ARG value is part of the cache key of every RUN step after its declaration,

177
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:39,433
because those steps can read it as an environment variable.

178
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:44,737
Declare the changing value as late as possible,

179
00:13:44,737 --> 00:13:49,826
and use it only where it is needed (a label, see Dockerfile.fixed):

180
00:13:51,567 --> 00:13:52,280
Got it.

181
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:55,031
What do I need to remember?

182
00:13:55,567 --> 00:13:58,703
One cache miss invalidates every later step:

183
00:13:58,703 --> 00:14:02,266
order steps from least to most frequently changed.

184
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:07,839
Copy dependency manifests before the code; copy the code last.

185
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:17,049
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=… keeps package manager caches between builds, outside the image.
